187
00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:53.299
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): Now, here's a better way. Keys. Instead of a password, you make a private key and a public key.

188
00:21:53.300 --> 00:22:08.109
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): You give the site your public key. Sure, anyone can see it, but your private key never leaves your device. When you log in, you sign a challenge with your private key. The site checks your signature with your public key, and that's it. You're in. That's how FIDO pass keys work.

189
00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:15.640
